---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Contact | Chip & Cell"
  description="How to reach Chip & Cell — corrections to data, questions about methodology, and everything else."
>
  <h1>Contact</h1>

  <p>
    Chip &amp; Cell is written and maintained by one person in Seoul, so replies are not
    instant — but every message is read.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p class="email"><a href="mailto:hello@chipandcell.com">hello@chipandcell.com</a></p>

  <h2>Reporting a data error</h2>
  <p>
    Corrections are the most useful mail we get. The pipeline pulls from KRX market data and
    public filings, and it does get things wrong. If a number looks off, send us:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>the page URL,</li>
    <li>the figure you think is wrong and what it should be, and</li>
    <li>where you checked it (exchange page, filing, data vendor).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We fix confirmed errors on the next pipeline run and note material corrections on the
    <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <p>
    We do not give personal investment advice, do not answer "should I buy X", and do not
    accept paid placements, sponsored posts or paid links in our coverage. See the
    <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .email { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  ul { line-height: 1.8; }
</style>
